{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/441304-2e-mating-beween-two-uratha","id":441304,"title":"2E - Mating beween two Uratha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-14T07:59:14-07:00","id":441304,"title":"2E - Mating beween two Uratha","content":"I haven't finished reading the book yet, but one of my players asked me and I thought of hitting the forums for it. Can two Uratha mate and bear children now? Or is just the taboo against two Uratha having intercourse what has been lifted? It's still not clear to me. Could someone help me out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:39:05-07:00","id":441347,"title":"","content":"They won't produce Unihar. The oath about cleaving to humanity is still important, but isn't explicit about relations between Uratha.<br /> <br /> I think it'd depend on the local Forsaken culture, IMO. Some places might be okay with it, others not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:08:08-07:00","id":441399,"title":"","content":"Oh, what I meant was if two Uratha mating can be <i>fertile</i> and have kids of their own, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:11:45-07:00","id":441402,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it works fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:12:20-07:00","id":441403,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> There's even a section about it, entitled Children of Wolves, with a subsection titled Pregnancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:08:02-07:00","id":441535,"title":"","content":"Is there a stated ratio of uratha breeding true to breeding wolf blooded? Something that always irked me about apocalypse was the absolutely dismal breeding numbers, unless you were a spiral. Then you can do whatever you want, and breed however much you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:14:45-07:00","id":441540,"title":"","content":"I don't think there was one given. I guess we'll need to tweak the numbers given in blood of the wolf to the new paradigm, so why not hash it out here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:25:18-07:00","id":441552,"title":"","content":"I would argue it's based on natural numbers, similar to how wolf populations go up or down by availability of resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:31:16-07:00","id":441555,"title":"","content":"It may be very difficult to determine because whether or not they become Uratha seems to be entirely arbitrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T11:51:16-07:00","id":441670,"title":"","content":"In the <b>Forsaken Chronicle Guide</b> Part 3 is whole chapter about romance, mating and pregnancy - and it is mostly cohesive with 2ed. I also agree with FCG look on Unihir as thing that is more of &quot;urban legend&quot;, but it is still a thing in modern Uratha society. &quot;You know, I heard that this poor couple from the pack on other side of town did not carrige normal child - but rather monsterous wolf spirit. But surley you and Jenn will be okay, yes?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T11:55:00-07:00","id":441671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/441304-2e-mating-beween-two-uratha?p=441535#post441535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a stated ratio of uratha breeding true to breeding wolf blooded? Something that always irked me about apocalypse was the absolutely dismal breeding numbers, unless you were a spiral. Then you can do whatever you want, and breed however much you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must also remember that you can become &quot;adopted&quot; Wolf-Blooded, i.e. the events changed you from human to WB. This influx should also have some part in numbers, especially by being bitten by Gauru ( and surviving ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T11:59:57-07:00","id":441673,"title":"","content":"Plus a lot of them get killed, reducing the population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T14:40:22-07:00","id":441854,"title":"","content":"Thanks, everyone! I see now there's much more options than before, and less arbitrary restrictions. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:30:07-07:00","id":442640,"title":"","content":"Makes me wonder about what needs to be done with the Matchmaker idigam now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:38:28-07:00","id":442646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/441304-2e-mating-beween-two-uratha?p=441552#post441552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue it's based on natural numbers, similar to how wolf populations go up or down by availability of resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why base it upon Wolf Populations and not Human Populations? That just sounds wonky to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T17:05:44-07:00","id":443312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/441304-2e-mating-beween-two-uratha?p=442640#post442640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes me wonder about what needs to be done with the Matchmaker idigam now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always thought it would be more creative if he ended up instead trying to create a mate from other spirits...humans...werewolves...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:13:00-07:00","id":452485,"title":"","content":"So I still don't quite get it. Are all werewolfs former Wolfblooded? How are wolfblooded born? Are the children of two werewolves wolfblooded and with the potential to become a werewolf? Is the child of a werewolf and a human wolfblooded? What about a human and a woldblooded? While I really like the new book and what was done to wolfblooded, I would like just one paragraf with clear explanations how Uratha are made. Maybe I'm just thick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5438-davaeorn","name":"Davaeorn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:26:55-07:00","id":452492,"title":"","content":"Being wolfblooded is not a requirement for undergoing the First Change, but it is <i>does</i> make it more likely.<br /> <br /> Now, in first edition, if I'm remembering correctly, the child of a werewolf was <i>always</i> wolfblooded, the child of two wolfbloods was <i>usually</i> wolfblooded, and the child of a wolfblood and a non-wolfblood was <i>sometimes</i> wolfblooded. Now that werewolves can safely breed with each other and wolfbloods are more potent in general that may well need shaking up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:31:12-07:00","id":452493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/441304-2e-mating-beween-two-uratha?p=452492#post452492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being wolfblooded is not a requirement for undergoing the First Change, but it is <i>does</i> make it more likely.<br /> <br /> Now, in first edition, if I'm remembering correctly, the child of a werewolf was <i>always</i> wolfblooded, the child of two wolfbloods was <i>usually</i> wolfblooded, and the child of a wolfblood and a non-wolfblood was <i>sometimes</i> wolfblooded. Now that werewolves can safely breed with each other and wolfbloods are more potent in general that may well need shaking up a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what does that mean? Can an ordinary human turn into a werewolf? I'm not saying I object, just a bit confused. Does it say anywhere what the offspring of two werewolves become?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5438-davaeorn","name":"Davaeorn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:45:12-07:00","id":452517,"title":"","content":"You can change without ever displaying a tell or being immune to lunacy. Whether that means you were a latent wolfblooded all along or not is a subject for debate, but the point is that &quot;ordinary&quot; folk can become werewolves out of the blue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:47:38-07:00","id":452520,"title":"","content":"Okay, fair enough. As for my other question, what does the offspring of werewolves become? Wolfblooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5438-davaeorn","name":"Davaeorn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T07:54:13-07:00","id":452688,"title":"","content":"I think of it like a recessive gene. You know the whole &quot;big B, little b&quot; thing they teach you about eye color to introduce the concept of alleles? The way I see it. you've got the dominant @big H&quot; marker for humans and the recessive &quot;little w&quot; marker for wolf-blooded. You need two little w's to be wolf-blooded, otherwise the dominant big H makes you human. So if both of your parents are human, you're most likely going to be human too, though there is a slight chance, if both of your parents have recessive little w's, that you might recieve them from both sides and be wolf-blooded. If one of your parents is wolf-blooded or a werewolf, you know you'll get a little w from them, but unless your human parent has a recessive little w <i>and</i> you recieve that from their side, you'll still be human. If both of your parents are full wolf-blooded or werewolves, you're definitely getting little w's from both sides, so you'll definitely be wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's probably way more complicated than that (hell, even eye color is actually way more complicated than that), but it illustrates the basic idea at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-22-2015, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:01:20-07:00","id":452690,"title":"","content":"The offspring of werewolves <i>may </i>be Wolf-Blooded but are not necessarily so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:13:42-07:00","id":452694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/441304-2e-mating-beween-two-uratha?p=452690#post452690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The offspring of werewolves <i>may </i>be Wolf-Blooded but are not necessarily so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, metaphysics. Always getting in the way of my attempts at pseudo-scientific explanations of supernatural things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T09:31:16-07:00","id":452765,"title":"","content":"I've never been one to resist technobabbly pseudoscientific metaphysics, so I figured out a way it might work. <br /> <br /> What you need is both a dominant and recessive werewolf gene, W and w, and a single human gene, H. HH is human, as is Hw, but HW is wolf blooded. Likewise WW and Ww are werewolf, but ww is wolfblooded. This means that a given werewolf will always be able to have werewolf, wolfblooded and human offspring depending on their partner, although admittedly some combinations will lack variety (WW + HH, I'm looking at you). Presumably Luna can step in there to shake things up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T09:45:51-07:00","id":452778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/441304-2e-mating-beween-two-uratha?p=452765#post452765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been one to resist technobabbly pseudoscientific metaphysics, so I figured out a way it might work. <br /> <br /> What you need is both a dominant and recessive werewolf gene, W and w, and a single human gene, H. HH is human, as is Hw, but HW is wolf blooded. Likewise WW and Ww are werewolf, but ww is wolfblooded. This means that a given werewolf will always be able to have werewolf, wolfblooded and human offspring depending on their partner, although admittedly some combinations will lack variety (WW + HH, I'm looking at you). Presumably Luna can step in there to shake things up a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the general idea, but people aren't born already werewolves. I assume in that case WW or Ww would be born wolf-blooded, but have the potential to undergo the first change at some point in their lives, while ww and HW wolf-blooded will never become full werewolves. Also there are &quot;the orphans&quot; throwing a wrench in the gears, and the whole idea makes it a little too easy for a geneticist to predict werewolf bloodlines and who will or won't have the potential to first change. But that's cool with me, I like having exceptions to my pseudoscientific theories. That's how you know there's magic involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-22-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T10:07:46-07:00","id":452794,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm thinking of slapping some probabilities in there with the stated phenome being the <i>most likely</i> outcome. Or maybe have W and w prone to randomly flipping or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T10:53:46-07:00","id":452845,"title":"","content":"Inheritance is a factor that shapes whether someone becomes a Wolf-Blooded or werewolf. There are other factors too, like exposure to Lunacy and how whimsical Luna is feeling, among other things.","signatur